    "visibleText": "What can we do for the Python community in Hong Kong in 2020? - PyCon HK Skip to content Menu PyCon HK Conference Highlights Schedule 2024 2023 2022 2021 2020 Fall 2020 Spring 2018 2017 2016 2015 Sponsors 2024 2023 2022 2021 2020 Fall 2018 2017 2016 2015 Communities 2024 2023 2022 Booths 2024 2023 Organizers 2024 2023 2022 Volunteers 2024 2023 2022 2021 2020 Fall 2018 2017 2016 2015 PyCon HK What can we do for the Python community in Hong Kong in 2020? Posted on April 29, 2020 July 20, 2025 What can we do for the Python community in Hong Kong in 2020? (Sammy Fung) (Hong Kong) is an English session in the online PyCon HK 2020 Spring. From the planning of PyCon HK 2020 in this fall, we discuss what can we do for the Python community for local and global in Hong Kong. Level: Beginner Speaker Bio: Sammy Fung Sammy is the organiser of PyCon Hong Kong, and one of the administrator of Hong Kong Python User Group facebook group. https://github.com/sammyfung https://hk.linkedin.com/in/sammyfung/ http://www.twitter.com/sammyfung https://sammyfun.com/ Session Time in HKT: 11:30 AM on 10 May 2020 Sunday. Session Time in GMT: 3:30 AM on 10 May 2020 Sunday. This session will be started right after the end of the session “ Decade of PyCon JP: How we spread the Python community in Japan (Takanori Suzuki) (Japan) ” at 11:00-11:30 AM in HKT. Related Session in Cantonese: 廣東話香港Python社群聚會 (Saturday 3:00 PM HKT) Instagram LinkedIn Facebook Twitter YouTube Search for: Archives Archives Select Month November 2024 October 2024 September 2024 July 2024 April 2024 December 2023 October 2023 September 2023 July 2023 April 2023 November 2022 October 2022 August 2022 October 2021 September 2021 May 2021 November 2020 October 2020 September 2020 May 2020 April 2020 November 2018 October 2018 September 2018 August 2018 November 2017 October 2016 November 2015 History 2026 2025 2024 2023 2022 2021 2020 Fall 2020 Spring 2020 2018 2017 2016 2015 ©2026 PyCon HK | Powered by SuperbThemes! ← Decade of PyCon JP: How we spread the Python community in Japan (Takanori Suzuki) (Japan) ← Fighting COVID-19 with Machine Learning"
