    "visibleText": "Apache Heron, the stream processing system, in Cybersecurity with Python - PyCon HK Skip to content Menu PyCon HK Conference Highlights Schedule 2024 2023 2022 2021 2020 Fall 2020 Spring 2018 2017 2016 2015 Sponsors 2024 2023 2022 2021 2020 Fall 2018 2017 2016 2015 Communities 2024 2023 2022 Booths 2024 2023 Organizers 2024 2023 2022 Volunteers 2024 2023 2022 2021 2020 Fall 2018 2017 2016 2015 PyCon HK Apache Heron, the stream processing system, in Cybersecurity with Python Posted on October 26, 2020 September 18, 2024 Apache Heron is a new competing stream processing system in the market. Originally developed by Twitter and used for tweet analytics, and later open-sourced to Apache Foundation. Combining with a streaming system for ingress and a database for storage, Apache Heron enables the ability of real-time big data analytic. With the native support of Python, Apache Heron allows developers to develop their stream processing system fully in Python without any additional library or binary required. In the Cybersecurity field, StormEye uses Apache Heron in Python for ingesting news feeds and data for Threat Intelligence, to provide an advanced feature for customers. Language: Cantonese Date & Time: 7 November 2020, Saturday 16:00-16:30 Speaker: Windham Wong Managed Partner of StormEye.io OSWE, OSCP, GCIA, Cybersecurity Specialist Committer of Apache Heron, Apache Incubating Project Member of The Apache SoftwareFoundation Website: https://stormeye.io Instagram LinkedIn Facebook Twitter YouTube Search for: Archives Archives Select Month November 2024 October 2024 September 2024 July 2024 April 2024 December 2023 October 2023 September 2023 July 2023 April 2023 November 2022 October 2022 August 2022 October 2021 September 2021 May 2021 November 2020 October 2020 September 2020 May 2020 April 2020 November 2018 October 2018 September 2018 August 2018 November 2017 October 2016 November 2015 History 2026 2025 2024 2023 2022 2021 2020 Fall 2020 Spring 2020 2018 2017 2016 2015 ©2026 PyCon HK | Powered by SuperbThemes! ← Build COVID-19 Chatbot with Python ← Building interactive map portal with GeoDjango"
