    "visibleText": "Develop Cloud-Native Application using MySQL Database Service - PyCon HK Skip to content Menu PyCon HK Conference Highlights Schedule 2024 2023 2022 2021 2020 Fall 2020 Spring 2018 2017 2016 2015 Sponsors 2024 2023 2022 2021 2020 Fall 2018 2017 2016 2015 Communities 2024 2023 2022 Booths 2024 2023 Organizers 2024 2023 2022 Volunteers 2024 2023 2022 2021 2020 Fall 2018 2017 2016 2015 PyCon HK Develop Cloud-Native Application using MySQL Database Service Posted on October 25, 2020 September 18, 2024 In this session, I will share about 2 topics: Developing cloud-native application development using Python with MySQL Database Service Implementing agile DevOps with MySQL docker containers on Kubernetes” Remark: I am providing first-hand information on our newly launched MySQL Database Service on Oracle Cloud (https://www.mysql.com/cloud/) as well as MySQL deployment on Kubernetes. I believe these topics will benefit Pycon’s attendees to understand more about the various options of working with MySQL Language: English Date & Time: 6 November 2020, Friday 14:50-15:20 Speaker: Ryan Kuan Oracle (MySQL) Malaysia/JAPAC Ryan Kuan is a Cloud Solution Architect of Oracle MySQL Global Business Unit, Asia Pacific, he provides solution design leadership to help customers on their digital transformation journey using MySQL and Oracle Cloud technology. Prior to joining Oracle MySQL, Ryan worked as Solution Architect in IBM assisting clients to adopt disruptive technologies such as Cloud, Big Data, SOA in their business transformation journey. Besides work, Ryan plays tennis actively, travels whenever he has free time and doodle mindlessly. Twitter: https://twitter.com/ryanckuan LinkedIn: https://www.linkedin.com/in/ryan-kuan/ Instagram LinkedIn Facebook Twitter YouTube Search for: Archives Archives Select Month November 2024 October 2024 September 2024 July 2024 April 2024 December 2023 October 2023 September 2023 July 2023 April 2023 November 2022 October 2022 August 2022 October 2021 September 2021 May 2021 November 2020 October 2020 September 2020 May 2020 April 2020 November 2018 October 2018 September 2018 August 2018 November 2017 October 2016 November 2015 History 2026 2025 2024 2023 2022 2021 2020 Fall 2020 Spring 2020 2018 2017 2016 2015 ©2026 PyCon HK | Powered by SuperbThemes! ← Python is your frend with MySQL Shell ← Python Debugging: Pro Tips and Not-So-Obvious Tricks"
