    "title": "Plug into JAX frameworks - PyCon HK",
    "description": "JAX is a library similar to NumPy, redesigned by Google for GPUs and TPUs. A wave of new ML frameworks, based on JAX, are looking for a chance to become an alternative to PyTorch and TensorFlow. In this session, I try out three JAX frameworks (Objax, Flax, and Elegy), showing the steps to solve Kaggle's",
